  "chapter": 519,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 35 Chapter 519\n\n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8102, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to employment\n        agencies\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  This bill would amend the General Business Law to modify the licensing\napplication  process  for employment agencies, clarify contract require-\nments between an employment  agency  and  a  job  seeker,  eliminate  an\nemployment  agency's  ability to charge a job seeker an advance fee, and\nenhance penalties for compliance failures.\n\n  I fully support the intent of this  bill.  Protecting  vulnerable  New\nYorkers  from predatory labor practices has been a hallmark of my admin-\nistration. As drafted, however, the  bill  contains  administrative  and\ntechnical  concerns  that  would  make  it extremely challenging, if not\nimpossible, to implement effectively in its present form.\n\n  The Executive has secured a three-way agreement with  the  Legislature\nto  pass  legislation in the upcoming session to address these concerns.\nOn that basis, I am singing this bill.\n\n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
